{"step_index":230,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T20:58:27Z","thinking":"**Identifying Frontend Connection Point**\n\nThe `EntityProfilePage.tsx` file clearly handles the entity display, receiving the entity `id` from URL parameters. Currently, it uses mock data. This file requires modification to fetch data from the `GET /api/entities/{id}` endpoint. The plan is to implement dynamic fetching with loading and error states, ensuring the UI updates when the `id` changes. A fallback to mock data or an error banner will be implemented for offline scenarios or API failures.\n\n\n**Defining API Interaction Points**\n\nImplementation will begin with a centralized API client for consistent data retrieval and error management. This client will encompass functions for all required endpoints, handling requests, responses, errors, and timeouts. UI components will incorporate loading and error states to provide feedback during data fetching. The error state will display messages and offer retry functionality.\n\nNext, `CasesPage.tsx` and other pages will be updated to use the new API client. These pages will handle loading and error states and provide fallbacks to prevent critical failures. The plan ensures that the UI functions gracefully even when the API is unreachable.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"npm run build","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Checking frontend build","toolSummary":"Run npm run build"}}]}
