{"step_index":232,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T20:59:01Z","thinking":"**Planning API Integration Implementation**\n\nThe request requires examining frontend files, determining necessary modifications, then implementing and testing an API connection. Focusing on the API implementation first seems prudent. The initial step involves creating a `api.ts` file within the specified directory. This file requires a configurable base URL and functions for handling specified endpoints (e.g., `GET /api/cases`).\n\n\n**Defining API Integration Requirements**\n\nThe next step involves defining the API contract and error handling. I need to create an `ApiError` class for consistent error management across components. This class should provide detailed messages, status codes and a method to check backend availability. It also involves outlining functions for each specified API endpoint (GET, POST, etc.) to handle requests and responses.\n\nThen, I need to connect the API with frontend components. Each of the components (CasesPage, DashboardPage, NetworkAnalysisPage, and EntityProfilePage) requires state management for loading, error handling, and data storage. Fetching data from the API and implementing error fallbacks with appropriate error banners are required for each page.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"/**\n * Central API Client for NEXUS Backend\n * Base URL: http://localhost:8000\n */\nimport { Case, Entity, NetworkGraphData, CrimePattern, ThreatAlert, MetricData } from '../types'\n\nexport const API_BASE_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL || 'http://localhost:8000'\n\nexport interface CaseInsightsResponse {\n  caseId: string\n  caseTitle: string\n  summary: string\n  patterns: CrimePattern[]\n  alerts: ThreatAlert[]\n  metrics: MetricData[]\n  dataset_label: string\n}\n\nexport interface HealthResponse {\n  status: string\n  service: string\n  version: string\n  timestamp: string\n  dataset: string\n  active_cases: number\n}\n\nexport class ApiError extends Error {\n  status: number\n  details?: unknown\n\n  constructor(message: string, status: number, details?: unknown) {\n    super(message)\n    this.name = 'ApiError'\n    this.status = status\n    this.details = details\n  }\n}\n\nasync function request<T>(endpoint: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const url = `${API_BASE_URL}${endpoint}`\n  const headers = {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    ...(options.headers || {}),\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(url, {\n      ...options,\n      headers,\n    })\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      let errorDetail = ''\n      try {\n        const errorJson = await response.json()\n        errorDetail = errorJson.error?.message || errorJson.detail || JSON.stringify(errorJson)\n      } catch {\n        errorDetail = response.statusText\n      }\n      throw new ApiError(\n        errorDetail || `API request failed with status ${response.status}`,\n        response.status\n      )\n    }\n\n    return (await response.json()) as T\n  } catch (err: unknown) {\n    if (err instanceof ApiError) {\n      throw err\n    }\n    const message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : 'Network error or backend unreachable'\n    throw new ApiError(\n      `Unable to connect to NEXUS Backend at ${API_BASE_URL}. (${message})`,\n      0\n    )\n  }\n}\n\nexport const api = {\n  // 1. Health Check\n  getHealth: async (): Promise<HealthResponse> => {\n    return request<HealthResponse>('/health')\n  },\n\n  // 2. Cases\n  getCases: async (params?: { status?: string; priority?: string; search?: string }): Promise<Case[]> => {\n    const query = new URLSearchParams()\n    if (params?.status && params.status !== 'ALL') query.append('status', params.status)\n    if (params?.priority && params.priority !== 'ALL') query.append('priority', params.priority)\n    if (params?.search) query.append('search', params.search)\n\n    const qs = query.toString()\n    return request<Case[]>(`/api/cases${qs ? `?${qs}` : ''}`)\n  },\n\n  getCaseById: async (caseId: string): Promise<Case> => {\n    return request<Case>(`/api/cases/${caseId}`)\n  },\n\n  createCase: async (caseData: {\n    title: string\n    description: string\n    codeName: string\n    priority?: string\n    leadInvestigator: string\n    agency?: string\n    jurisdiction?: string\n  }): Promise<Case> => {\n    return request<Case>('/api/cases', {\n      method: 'POST',\n      body: JSON.stringify(caseData),\n    })\n  },\n\n  // 3. Network Graph (Powered by NetworkX)\n  getNetwork: async (caseId: string, filterType?: string): Promise<NetworkGraphData> => {\n    const qs = filterType ? `?filter_type=${encodeURIComponent(filterType)}` : ''\n    return request<NetworkGraphData>(`/api/network/${caseId}${qs}`)\n  },\n\n  // 4. Entities\n  getEntity: async (entityId: string): Promise<Entity> => {\n    return request<Entity>(`/api/entities/${entityId}`)\n  },\n\n  getEntities: async (city?: string): Promise<Entity[]> => {\n    const qs = city ? `?city=${encodeURIComponent(city)}` : ''\n    return request<Entity[]>(`/api/entities${qs}`)\n  },\n\n  // 5. Insights\n  getInsights: async (caseId: string): Promise<CaseInsightsResponse> => {\n    return request<CaseInsightsResponse>(`/api/insights/${caseId}`)\n  },\n}\n","Description":"Create central API client for NEXUS backend","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Nityam Jaiswal\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexus\\src\\lib\\api.ts","toolAction":"Writing api.ts","toolSummary":"Create nexus/src/lib/api.ts"}}]}
